10. Predictive Corrective Action Management
Finding a hazard is only the first step.

The real question is whether the organization actually controls it.

A predictive safety system can analyse:

Open corrective actions
Overdue actions
Repeat findings
Action severity
Responsible departments
Closure times
Verification results
This helps identify where corrective-action processes themselves may be becoming a risk.

For example, if the same type of corrective action repeatedly remains overdue across several sites, the organization may need to address the underlying management process rather than simply sending another reminder.

This is where connected CAPA management becomes an important part of predictive safety.

